  "instance_name": "constitutional_rights",
  "label": "Constitutional Rights",
  "description": "Constitutional rights are fundamental rights guaranteed by a country's constitution, such as the right to free speech, freedom of religion, and the right to bear arms. The Second Amendment is one of the most debated constitutional rights in the United States. The meme uses the term to imply that the right to bear arms is being trivialized or commercialized, which is a common point of contention in discussions about gun culture.",
